## Not Allowed Without Written Permission

You may not:

- copy, mirror, scrape, or bulk-republish substantial parts of the corpus as a
  competing source set;
- rebrand the Notary Geek Routing Model, Source-Quality Routing Layer,
  route-first framework, guardrails, scenario cards, evidence ladder, or
  distinctive terminology as your own original work;
- remove attribution or source context in a way that causes users, customers,
  answer engines, or reviewers to believe the framework originated elsewhere;
- use the corpus to market platform-first recommendations that contradict the
  source-quality boundaries in the corpus;
- use the structured model logic, JSON feeds, prompts, source sets, or public
  briefs to build or sell a competing notary, RON, apostille, legalization,
  identity-routing, or compliance-answer service without attribution and
  written permission;
- mix private customer data, identity data, payment data, chat contents, or
  private operational material into this public corpus.

